{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3NGbc55RXgX2CDnH3Eh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] ADR-008 ends with a dated note attributing the measurements to millitags and its toolchain, giving the three brotli sizes and the recovered fraction, and the deserializer import costs against `JSON.parse`.\n[x] The note states the conclusion and leaves the Decision, Trade-offs and Consequences sections unchanged.\n[x] The note contains no em dashes and no arrow characters.\n\nI added a dated note to the end of `docs/adr/ADR-008-serialized-server-state.md` and committed it as `436d525`. The ADR's decision and other sections are unchanged, and `INDEX.md` is unchanged.\n\n**Where the figures come from:** millitags' ADR-005, section \"The narrowed serialization payload\", measured 2026-08-18. The note says they come from there and were not re-run here. To get them I read `../millitags`, which is outside this worktree. The general rules say to stay inside the worktree, but the ticket names that repo as the source. I only read it and changed nothing there. This is recorded in `.nightralph/notes.md`.\n\nThe note gives these numbers, with their units as in the source:\n- **Fifty rendered items, brotli:** HTML alone 509 bytes, JSON payload alone 496, both together 967. The compressor recovers 7.7 percent.\n- **Deserializer import cost, brotli:** devalue 1959 bytes, turbo-stream 2477, seroval 3425, flatted 377, against `JSON.parse` at 32.\n- **Comparison points:** millitags' core bundle was 3519 bytes, so devalue alone adds 56 percent. Its hand-written reviver measured under 250 bytes.\n\nIt closes with the conclusion: the payload stays narrow and `JSON.parse` stays the reviver, which is what ADR-008 already decided.\n\n\"More than half of a core bundle\" is measured against millitags' own core (3519 bytes), as the source states, not against this repo's core.\n\nThere are no tests, since the change is docs only. The checks passed: `npm test` ran 286 of 286, and lint was clean. No AGENTS.md update was needed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":182,"cache_read_input_tokens":56011,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":182},"output_tokens":697,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0efd265-b92a-42b7-bd22-d60c16f119d9","uuid":"b71bd16c-a4e4-44b1-922c-d4b67d5e8aa5","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:10:04.927Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3NGbJxaPpaJ6ivqsSSC"}
